# Copy to server/.env (git-ignored) and fill in. Provider keys live only here, never on a device.
# How Cubey hears and speaks: cascade (default) through Soniox and a model; live, speech to speech on Gemini Live
# (gemini-3.8-live). Gemini's terms forbid apps used by under-18s: an open question before any child talks to Cubey
# (docs/design.md).
# CUBEY_TALK=cascade
# Talking over Cubey while it speaks: on unless 0 (the device's detector can take a loud room for her).
# CUBEY_TALK_OVER=0
# Gemini Live (live), or the model below if it is Gemini's.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Soniox's speech-to-text and text-to-speech (cascade).
SONIOX_API_KEY=
# The model between them (cascade): OpenAI's gpt-6-sol by default, or Gemini's (gemini-3.1-flash-lite, with GEMINI_API_KEY).
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# CUBEY_MODEL=gpt-6-sol
# The models for the games with words (and her word game), and for drawing on Cubey's screen.
# CUBEY_SMART_MODEL=gpt-6-sol
# CUBEY_DRAW_MODEL=gpt-6-astra
# The admin page (/admin): every Cubey, its child, its talks, what it cost. Without a password, no page.
CUBEY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# No child here: each Cubey's is its own (memory.md in CUBEY_DATA/devices/<id>/), got to know by talking (their name,
# their age), its languages set on its menu (a new Cubey's opens by itself), all of it on the admin page.
# Where the household lives, for the time of day a new Cubey knows (the server's own if unset; Fly's is UTC).
# CUBEY_CHILD_TIMEZONE=Europe/Riga

# The server listens on this Mac only (the simulator). For a device on the network set HOST=0.0.0.0 and a long
# random CUBEY_DEVICE_TOKEN (openssl rand -hex 32), which every device must then send.
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# CUBEY_DEVICE_TOKEN=
